      "A/B NetCDF compression level 1 versus the current level 4, including HICAR read time and storage; the current regular writer is single-core CPU-bound for about 107 s.",
      "Compile or batch-vectorize reconstruct_column_state while preserving per-column arithmetic; its Python loop is the largest measured phase.",
      "Cache cycle-invariant ICON HHL and target/static geometry across hourly records in a multi-record worker; do not change the serialized forcing contract until HICAR reader behavior is separately qualified."
    ],
    "not_recommended_as_default": "Raising column workers from 8 to 16 solely for throughput. It saves about 143 s per record but nearly exhausts node memory and increases total CPU."
